  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Added\n- **Button answers in scenes.** `ctx.Ask` / `ctx.Ask<T>` now accept `choices:` and render the answers as an inline keyboard; the tapped button answers the step and is parsed into `T` exactly like a typed reply. Build the set with `AskChoices.ForEnum<TEnum>()` (one button per member, captions from `[Description]` or a `Func<TEnum, string>` you supply), `AskChoices.Of(...)` for free-form values/labels, `.InColumns(n)` for layout and `.Keep()` to leave the keyboard in place. Typed replies still work and match a choice by value or label. Each keyboard is stamped with the scene step it answers, so a tap on a stale keyboard re-asks that question instead of answering the current one; an accepted tap clears the keyboard and answers the callback query.\n- `TestBot.TapButtonLabeled(\"💎 Pro\")` taps an inline button by caption, so scene keyboards can be driven in tests without hand-writing callback data.\n\n### Changed\n- Scenes now also intercept taps on the buttons their own `Ask` prompts rendered (callback data prefixed `kpa:`). Ordinary `[CallbackQuery]` handlers and commands are unaffected and still route normally during a scene.\n- `SceneContext.Ask` gained optional parameters (`Ask(string, AskChoices?)`, `Ask<T>(string, string?, AskChoices?)`). Source-compatible; recompile against 1.3.0 rather than swapping the assembly in place.",
